# Atlas Tests and Review Rules

- Every feature needs meaningful tests.
- Every AI behavior change needs eval or smoke test coverage.
- Every permission change needs leakage tests.
- PRs must be linked to issues.
- PRs must explain what, why, how, tests, risks, and learning.
- Keep PRs small and reviewable.
- Use Conventional Commits.
- Do not approve PRs that authors cannot explain.
- Provider/env changes need `.env.example`, provider docs, and doctor/env check coverage.
- For bug fixes, reproduce the bug as close to the end-user experience as practical before fixing.
- Be strict about rendered UI quality during E2E and preview review.
- Do not ignore lint, type, test, or flaky-test failures; fix them or create a tracked issue with evidence.
